Subject: [flux] Name the user-visible install paths Flux

kProductPathName is what Windows builds the user data directory from, so an
unpatched fork writes to %LOCALAPPDATA%\Chromium\User Data - the same place a
real Chromium install uses. Two browsers sharing one profile directory is not
a cosmetic problem.

base_app_name and base_app_id go with it: they are what Windows shows for the
app and what the taskbar groups windows by, so leaving them meant Flux windows
grouping under Chromium.

Deliberately NOT changed here:

- The ProgID prefixes and descriptions (ChromiumHTM, "Chromium PDF Document").
  They are file-association identity, which only matters once there is an
  installer to register them, and there is not one yet.
- The CLSIDs and GUIDs. They identify the elevation and tracing services to
  COM. Changing them is correct for a fork that installs system-wide, but it
  is only meaningful alongside an installer, and a half-changed set is worse
  than an unchanged one.
- kSafeBrowsingName. It identifies the client to Google's Safe Browsing
  service, which is inert in this fork - dev.gn ships no API keys.

--- a/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
+++ b/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 // The brand-specific product name to be included as a component of the install
 // and user data directory paths.
-inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Chromium";
+inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Flux";
 
 // The brand-specific safe browsing client name.
 inline constexpr char kSafeBrowsingName[] = "chromium";
@@ -45,8 +45,8 @@
         .logo_suffix = L"",  // No logo suffix for the primary install mode.
         .app_guid =
             L"",  // Empty app_guid since no integration with Google Update.
-        .base_app_name = L"Chromium",              // A distinct base_app_name.
-        .base_app_id = L"Chromium",                // A distinct base_app_id.
+        .base_app_name = L"Flux",                  // A distinct base_app_name.
+        .base_app_id = L"Flux",                    // A distinct base_app_id.
         .browser_prog_id_prefix = L"ChromiumHTM",  // Browser ProgID prefix.
         .browser_prog_id_description =
             L"Chromium HTML Document",  // Browser ProgID description.
